            <ArticleTitle>The Immune System in Cancer Pathogenesis: Potential Therapeutic Approaches.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>4273943</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1155/2016/4273943</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Interplay among immune activation and cancer pathogenesis provides the framework for a novel subspecialty known as immunooncology. In the rapidly evolving field of immunooncology, understanding the tumor-specific immune response enhances understanding of cancer resistance. This review highlights the fundamentals of incorporating precision medicine to discover new immune biomarkers and predictive signatures. Using a personalized approach may have a significant, positive impact on the use of oncolytics to better guide safer and more effective therapies.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
